---
description: "NestJS backend rules (SOLID/DDD-lite, testing, error contracts)"
globs:
  - "apps/api/**/*.ts"
  - "src/backend/**/*.ts"
  - "**/*.controller.ts"
  - "**/*.service.ts"
  - "**/*.module.ts"
alwaysApply: false
---

# NestJS Backend Rules
- Keep controllers thin: validation + delegation only.
- Business logic must live in services/use-cases.
- Prefer dependency inversion: depend on interfaces when a boundary exists (db, external services).
- Define a consistent error contract (status, message, code).
- Avoid boolean-flag parameters in services; prefer objects or strategies.
- Add tests for new behavior (happy path + 2 edge cases).
